  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "Drops can be chained, so one records that it follows another. That link is set up earlier than you might expect."
    },
    {
      "t": 7.75,
      "text": "We already have one sealed drop here, and the ledger shows what it ended up with."
    },
    {
      "t": 12.88,
      "text": "This is where we read the value the next drop has to point at."
    },
    {
      "t": 17.04,
      "text": "When we create the next drop, we say up front which one it follows, carrying that value over."
    },
    {
      "t": 23.52,
      "text": "Then it is an ordinary drop. Stage what belongs in it."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "Close it with its own nonce, each drop has its own, not the parent's."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "And there is the parent line, pointing back at the drop we came from."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "And you cannot invent the value: zep only accepts one it has actually sealed."
    },
    {
      "t": 46.35,
      "text": "The link is declared when the drop is created, and only a real anchor will do."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that the parent is declared at creation from the parent's anchor, and that zep validates the anchor."
}
